            <ArticleTitle>[Hypophyseal-gonadal and hypophyseal-corticoadrenal system in healthy persons and in patients with ischemic heart disease aged 60-89 years].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>52-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Serum basal concentrations of testosterone, estradiol, and androstenedione, FSH, LH, prolactin, ACTH and cortisol were studied in healthy persons, CHD patients aged 60-89, and in healthy persons aged 20-35 (controls). In some persons of each group a study was made of changes in the concentration of blood prolactin. ACTH, cortisol and urinary excretion of free cortisol as a result of bicycle ergometry exercise testing (submaximum in healthy persons and threshold in patients). A conclusion was made that &quot;endocrinological age&quot; of these hormonal systems in CHD patients aged 60-89 was older than in healthy persons of similar age, and hormonal imbalance continued to be a risk factor at late stages of life.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
